  {
   "id": "d964bf30-cab8-47a1-bf23-aa8fb96c3b97",
   "term": "Maximum SPL",
   "verdict": "MINOR",
   "suggestions": [
    {
     "field": "plain_english",
     "severity": "Medium",
     "issue": "The definition names 'microphone, speaker, or audio device,' but every teaching element (plain_english, practical, all scenarios, mistakes) is exclusively about a microphone's input handling ('read the mic's Max SPL,' 'capsule,' 'pad'). A beginner is left to conflate a mic's max INPUT it can capture cleanly with a loudspeaker's max OUTPUT it can produce — two distinct senses of the same spec — which is a real common misconception.",
     "suggestion": "Add one clause distinguishing the senses, e.g. 'For a microphone this is the loudest input it can capture without distorting; for a loudspeaker it is the highest output level it can produce cleanly.' Either that or scope the entry to the microphone sense so the definition and examples match."
    }
   ]
